WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.124
NARRATOR: The social worker
answers directly.

2
00:00:06.124 --> 00:00:10.766
She explains that her role is to
assess Dr. Osei's capacity to decide

3
00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:14.878
where she lives, that capacity
is specific to that decision,

4
00:00:14.878 --> 00:00:17.688
and that no one has
decided anything yet.

5
00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:18.971
DR. OSEI: Thank you.

6
00:00:19.171 --> 00:00:22.085
That is the first straight answer
I have had in a month.

7
00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:24.398
Then let me give you what you
need.

8
00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:28.737
The neurologist's report is in that
drawer; the MRI was unremarkable for my
age.

9
00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.885
The pharmacy prints
my medication list,

10
00:00:30.885 --> 00:00:33.529
and I check it against
the bottles every Sunday.

11
00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:36.990
I will also tell you what I have
not told my son.

12
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:39.450
Twice this year I have had trouble
with words.

13
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:40.992
Names, mostly.

14
00:00:41.192 --> 00:00:44.559
It frightened me enough that I
booked the neurologist myself.

15
00:00:44.559 --> 00:00:46.457
I would rather you hear
that from me

16
00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:49.092
than discover it and wonder
what else I am hiding.

17
00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:50.551
Now.

18
00:00:50.751 --> 00:00:54.766
If your assessment finds that I can
decide, will he be told that in writing?

19
00:00:56.166 --> 00:01:00.430
NARRATOR: Dr. Osei has disclosed a
concern she has kept from her son.

20
00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.782
What has your candor made
possible, and how do you respond?
